(
control_mesh_gid_batch (manual Professional 6.200) with gid on the PATH.
build_safe.sh runs this test in a scratch copy with a fake gid script first
on the PATH: called as "gid -n -b GidMeshBatch.bch", it writes
mesh_gid.gid/mesh_gid.dat (4 tria3 elements in the unit square, middle
node 5 at 0.5 0.5), as the tochnog.gid problem type does. Tochnog copies
that file to 10.dat, removes GidMeshBatch.bch and the mesh_gid.gid
directory, and control_input 10 reads the mesh in the same control index
(the Professional 02-08-2026 does the same with this fake gid). The target
checks node 5 of the mesh read.
)
echo -no
number_of_space_dimensions 2
materi_velocity
materi_displacement
end_initia
mesh_gid_point_coord 1 0. 0.
mesh_gid_point_coord 2 1. 0.
mesh_gid_point_coord 3 0. 1.
mesh_gid_point_coord 4 1. 1.
mesh_gid_line_point 1 1 2
mesh_gid_line_point 2 2 4
mesh_gid_line_point 3 4 3
mesh_gid_line_point 4 3 1
mesh_gid_surface_line 1 1 2 3 4
mesh_gid_surface_element_group 1 1
mesh_gid_assign_conditions_line 11 1
mesh_gid_size 0.5
control_mesh_gid_batch 10 -yes
control_input 10 -yes
target_item 0 -node 5 1
target_value 0 0.5 1.e-8
end_data
